Check In :: Title of the screen where the person says how they feel after a dose. It is not a hotel or flight check-in.
Check in :: Label of the tappable control on a dose row that opens the Check In screen. It is not a hotel or flight check-in.
Dose :: A noun: one taken amount of a medication.
Log dose :: Button that opens the Log Dose screen. "Log" is a verb.
Log Dose :: Title of the screen where the person records a dose they took. "Log" is a verb.
Pin :: Verb on a swipe button: keep a place as a quick choice on the New Entry screen. It is not a map pin.
Pinned :: Spoken when a place becomes a quick choice, and the state of such a place. It is not a map pin.
Unpinned :: Spoken when a place stops being a quick choice. It is not a map pin.
Left :: The left side of the body, not a direction.
Right :: The right side of the body, not a direction.
Manage :: Verb: button on the Log Dose screen that opens the list of medications, to add, archive or restore them.
Archive :: Verb: hides the medication from the list but keeps the history of its doses.
More actions :: Accessibility label of the button drawn as three dots that opens a menu of further actions.
Save :: Verb: primary button of every form. It stores what the form holds, such as an entry, a dose or a medication.
